= GeoTracker – Android Fitness Tracking App =

== Current Status ==

GeoTracker is a professional-grade Android fitness tracking application for serious athletes, outdoor users, and multi-sport training. It combines high-precision GPS/GNSS recording, sensor collection, live web sharing, route analysis, event planning, and local-first data management.

Current source version: **11.05**, dated **2026-10-14** in the Android build configuration. The current local database is **Room v31** with **17 entities**.

Documentation updated **2026-10-23**, checked against repository commit **56075cd** and the implementation history from April through October 2026. This describes the checked-in application; the installed phone and server versions may differ.

{{toc start="2" depth="3"/}}

The app targets runners, cyclists, hikers, skaters, winter sport users, swimmers, multi-sport athletes, and people who want detailed performance insight beyond basic distance/time statistics.

== Supported Activity Types and Modes ==

* Running
** Trail Running
** Road Running
** Track Running
** Orienteering
** Backyard Ultra
** Wings for Life Run
* Cycling with detailed bicycle configuration
* Hiking
* Water Sports
** Swimming - Open Water
** Kayaking
** Canoeing
** Stand Up Paddleboarding
* Winter Sport
** Ski
** Snowboard
** Cross Country Skiing
** Ski Touring
** Biathlon
** Sledding
** Snowshoeing
** Ice Hockey
* Skating
** Inline Skating
* Multisport Race
** Duathlon
** Triathlon
** Ultratriathlon
* Fitness Test
** Lactate Threshold (30min TT)
* Indoor/time-based activities, including Weight Training and other activities where GPS is not required

=== Sport Classification and Recording Modes ===

Activities store a **sport family**, optional **discipline**, and optional **event format** separately. Running includes Road Running, Trail Running, Track Running, and Orienteering. Legacy names such as Half Marathon and Ultramarathon are recognized and migrated to the structured metadata.

Distance and timed milestones are calculated from recorded data. You do not need to select Marathon, Half Marathon, or a timed ultra category before recording. **Backyard Ultra** and **Wings for Life Run** remain special choices because they change recording behavior. Sport metadata is preserved during editing, recovery, REST synchronization, and WebSocket transfer.

== Key Android App Features ==

=== GPS and Location Tracking ===

* High-precision GPS/GNSS tracking with satellite quality monitoring
* Intelligent GPS signal quality evaluation and GPS anomaly filtering
* Dual altitude tracking: GPS altitude and barometric pressure altitude
* Slope percentage calculation and terrain analysis
* Real-time speed, moving speed, maximum speed, distance, bearing, and accuracy metrics
* Start and end location reverse geocoding with city, country, and address
* Configurable recording behavior with battery-conscious background services
* Crash/session recovery that preserves accumulated distance and reuses the current event after service or app restarts
* Stable recording after background-service handoff, including fixes for timer/distance freezes and stale foreground metrics

=== Recording Reliability and Completed Activities ===

* GPS startup monitoring detects missing or stalled callbacks and performs bounded recovery attempts. Background-to-foreground service handoff and location-listener races have been corrected.
* Reverse geocoding runs outside the recording persistence loop, with a timeout, so a stalled address lookup cannot freeze recording.
* After stopping, the completed route, waypoints, and statistics remain visible and can be restored when returning to the Map tab. Starting a new recording or loading an event updates the displayed activity.
* A green start flag marks the first recorded GPS point; a checkered finish flag appears after recording stops. Flags are restored for saved events and remain distinguishable when endpoints overlap.
* Duplicate GPS coordinates and stationary tracks no longer break route-gradient rendering. Route drawing errors are isolated from map fallback behavior.
* Live weather refreshes every five minutes; the latest weather remains available when opening Statistics later during a recording and is cleared between sessions.
* Unavailable pressure readings are represented as missing data instead of zero measurements.
* WebSocket connections and reconnects are skipped when transfer is disabled or the server address is blank or the legacy 0.0.0.0 placeholder. Invalid addresses cannot crash recording startup.

=== Sensor Data Collection ===

* Bluetooth LE heart rate monitor support
* Heart rate zones, heart rate trends, and HR correlation charts
* Running cadence from Android step-detector events, displayed in steps per minute (SPM), plus stride length tracking
* Cadence stored per metric, included in GPX-compatible exports, and transmitted through WebSocket and REST synchronization
* Cycling-compatible cadence values displayed in cycles per minute when present; this does not imply automatic bicycle cadence measurement from the phone step detector
* Step counting via device sensors
* Barometric pressure sensing with QNH-based sea-level calibration
* Temperature and weather data handling, including true zero-degree values instead of placeholder filtering
* User profile fields for height, weight, birth date, max heart rate, and automatically calculated BMI
* BMI persistence in settings, Room user data, metrics payloads, WebSocket messages, and server-side history

=== Real-Time Tracking UI ===

* OpenStreetMap-based live tracking map with dark mode support
* Satellite/street map toggle
* Speed-colored routes
* Slope-colored route visualization
* Direction arrows along recorded tracks
* Waypoints and waypoint photo support
* Bottom-sheet metrics only on the Map tab, keeping other tabs cleaner
* Recording controls stay available while following other users
* Session start time and elapsed duration in the live speed panel
* Home-screen widget with duration, distance, speed, altitude, temperature, barometer, total activity time, and inactivity timer
* Split/lap table in the live panel
* Live route continuity after app restart during recording

=== Special Recording Modes ===

* Pause/resume without losing session data
* Manual and automatic lap timing
* Backyard Ultra mode with manual lap handling and fixed lap-distance tracking
* Multisport race support for Duathlon, Triathlon, and Ultratriathlon with discipline transitions
* Wings for Life Run mode with the virtual catcher-car schedule, live map position, distance/headway comparison, catch announcements, and catch-point details while recording continues
* Lactate Threshold fitness test:
** Requires a connected heart rate sensor
** Runs a 30-minute time trial protocol
** Uses a settle-in phase and measurement phase
** Collects HR and speed samples during the last 20 minutes
** Auto-stops at 30 minutes
** Calculates average LTHR and LT pace
** Supports early stop with partial result calculation
** Shows countdown and result dialogs

== Event Management ==

=== My Events ===

* Searchable event history
* Events sorted newest-first
* Event cards with route preview mini-map
* Read-only OSMDroid mini-map preview with start/end markers and automatic bounds fitting
* Long route preview downsampling to keep memory usage bounded
* Start/end location display
* Event comments and clothing fields
* Edit event screen with sport type, metadata, comments, clothing, and synchronization fields
* Connect Events feature to merge multiple recorded events into one event, combining locations, metrics, laps, waypoints, media, discipline transitions, clothing, and network information
* Fastest lap calculation that ignores incomplete final laps
* Event source tracking to distinguish recorded events from imported Ghost Racer tracks; Ghost Racers are excluded from yearly activity statistics

=== Stage Groups and All Stages Analysis ===

Separate recordings can belong to a named stage group, for example the days of a multi-day tour or race. This preserves individual recordings; **Connect Events** remains available for creating a single merged event.

To organize stages:

1. Edit an event and set **Stage group (optional)**.
1. Enter a **Stage number**, or leave it empty for automatic numbering.
1. Assign the other recordings to the same group; **Choose existing group** selects a saved name. Clear the group field to remove one event from its group.
1. In Events, use **Group stage events** to switch grouped display on or off. Group cards provide an overview and member-event access. **Ungroup recordings** removes the grouping while keeping the recordings.
1. Open stage analysis and choose **This stage** or **All stages**. Tap a stage-comparison row to inspect that individual stage.

**All stages** displays colored stage routes on one map, speed and altitude charts across cumulative distance, combined distance and recorded time, average and maximum speed, ascent/descent totals, and a stage comparison table. Each chart line represents one stage; gaps between stages are not joined. Recorded time includes stops within a stage and excludes gaps between stages. The October update improves the combined analysis layout and scrolling.

=== Events Toolbar and Navigation ===

Toolbar actions are grouped under **Calendar**, **Statistics**, **Server**, and **Tools**, with short descriptions and destructive actions highlighted in red. Removing calendar exports keeps the GeoTracker recordings. The obsolete invalid-event cleanup feature and duplicate Events-tab slope legend have been removed. Lap analysis has a back button, and returning from analysis preserves the expanded event and its loaded details.

=== Media and Sharing ===

* Attach image and video media to events
* Local media storage with thumbnails
* Full-screen image viewing with pinch-to-zoom
* Video playback via external player
* Pending upload indicators and retry-capable media synchronization
* Server-side session media storage
* Server-generated thumbnails for images and video
* Media upload support for live-streamed WebSocket events
