=== Cadence Analysis and Statistics Loading ===

Expanded event cards include average cadence and a preview graph. Dedicated cadence analysis provides minimum, average, and maximum values with interactive cadence-versus-time, distance, altitude, and speed charts and a map for the selected sample.

The Event Overview statistics screen reports calculation progress through Activities, Trends, Heart Rate, and SPM phases. Running summaries include minimum/average/maximum SPM, monthly cadence trends, and cadence distribution charts. Statistics queries load the full event history.

=== Achievements and Personal Bests ===

The **Achievements** screen combines sport-family personal bests with the activity summary. Running distance records cover **1 km, 5 km, 10 km, half marathon (21.0975 km), marathon (42.195 km), 50 km, and 100 km**. Timed efforts include **6, 12, 24, 48, and 72 hours, and 6 days**.

Milestones are calculated independently from recorded metrics, regardless of the event format selected before recording. Invalid or missing timestamps, discontinuous timed-record windows, and implausible distance jumps are excluded to prevent false records from damaged imports.

Selecting a week in the activity summary opens the main Events screen filtered to that **ISO week**, sport, and multisport discipline where applicable. The active filter is visible; choose **Show All Events** to clear it. ISO-week grouping handles year boundaries correctly.

=== Lap Grouping and Cumulative Time ===

Android and web analysis offer a lap-count selector to combine consecutive laps. Time, distance, and pace are recalculated from actual grouped totals rather than assuming one kilometre per lap. Map and graph filtering follows the grouped selection. Incomplete groups are excluded from fastest/slowest highlighting. Android Lap Times includes a **Total** column for cumulative elapsed lap time, including grouped laps.

