* Cadence in chart hover popups with sport-specific units; partial messages preserve the latest cadence
* Cadence mini-chart restored from the last five minutes of history using recorded timestamps, rolling averages, and missing-data gaps
* Session start time and duration display
* Heart rate chart alongside altitude and speed charts
* Toggleable altitude overlay on the heart rate chart
* Correct nearest-session chart hover behavior for multi-session display
* Chart resize handling through ResizeObserver
* Chart zoom and pan support with Chart.js zoom plugin and Hammer.js
* Double-click chart zoom reset
* Panel resizing and compact panel-header navigation
* Fixed live-session list behavior for reset recording fragments
* Reset recording fragments merged in live UI

=== Redis Live History and Session Consistency ===

**PostgreSQL** is the durable activity store. **Redis** caches the rolling live-tracking history, with a default **48-hour** retention window controlled by DATA_RETENTION_HOURS. Historical analysis remains backed by PostgreSQL.

* Session Manager and graphs use the same Redis history snapshot.
* Cleanup broadcasts the updated session list; expired browser routes, charts, map elements, and statistics are removed together.
* Local browser history and name refreshes do not resurrect expired sessions.
* After service restart, an empty Redis cache can be backfilled from recent PostgreSQL points with their original timestamps. Existing cache history is preserved.
* Live sessions reload after WebSocket restart, and reset fragments remain one logical route.
* Session names use the saved database name matched by session ID. Connected browsers refresh names every five seconds; cached tracking points cannot overwrite renamed events.
* Docker Compose includes Redis startup/health checks and shared network configuration.

